__pycache__
.claude
.cachebro
old*
cpm
*.pt
*.COM
*.com
*.TAP
*.tap
*.bin
packages/
dist/
# The MediaWiki dump itself, which data/wikipedia/README.md tells you to fetch
# into this directory. 338MB, and every byte of it is on dumps.wikimedia.org.
*.xml.bz2

# Built from a MediaWiki dump by data/wikipedia/ingest.py - ~110MB, and
# reproducible from any snapshot, so it is not worth a git object. The -wal
# and -shm sidecars are SQLite's, and appear whenever the database is opened.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# The Wikidata truthy dump, the graph data/wikipedia/wikidata.py --build makes
# from it, and the parquet it stages on the way. Tens of GB each; the dump is
# on dumps.wikimedia.org and everything downstream of it is reproducible.
*.nt.bz2
*.lbdb
*.lbdb.wal
*.parquet

# What --export cuts that graph down to. A few MB and cheap to remake, but it
# is derived data and it carries the name of the dump it came from.
wikidata.tsv.gz

# Question sets fetched from their upstreams by data/questions/*.py, which
# record the URLs they came from.
data/questions/cache/
*.IDX
*.DAT
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Coverage output; the report is a CI step summary, not a committed file.
.coverage
coverage.json
coverage.txt
htmlcov/
